From 78fcb6d28756695015ace1edee74bc7b6aa9cb19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gg582 <gg582@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:39:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: full t8103 bring-up sequence (macOS + m1n1
 RE parity)

Replicate the complete t8103 AVD bring-up that the upstream driver never
performed (it relied on hardware defaults / boot-chain state, which holds
on j274 but not on j293 where the CM3 never sets FLAG0):

- map the full 0x268000000 aperture (Apple DT single-window layout)
- ADS block power (0x269000000 = 0xfff, macOS DevicePwrOn) and the
  macOS waitValidADSStatus poll ((status & 0x7f0) == 0x7f0)
- dart-avd init masks 0x269010060/68/6c (m1n1 fw/avd + macOS agree)
- clear SRAM (macOS clearDMEM)
- CAvdWrapCtrlViola::DeviceInit writes (wrap + IRQ clears)
- DMA stage0 tunables table (~150 registers)
- mcpu start: +0x10 = 2 mailbox interrupt enable before RUN_CTRL
  (was missing; m1n1 RE sequence and macOS disasm agree)
- AVDBG: ADS status, pmgr ps dump around avd_sys, ADS on timeout

Sources: AppleAVD.kext v865 arm64e disasm (fox-builder-macos docs) and
m1n1 proxyclient/m1n1/fw/avd/__init__.py (original bring-up RE).
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c  |  10 +
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hw.c   | 231 +++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-regs.h |  25 +++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h      |   2 +
 4 files changed, 260 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
index 643e788a5..0c379d5aa 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
@@ -717,6 +717,16 @@ static int avd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(avd->ctrl))
 		return PTR_ERR(avd->ctrl);
 
+	/* Map the full AVD aperture (Apple DT layout: one window at
+	 * 0x268000000) so the t8103 preinit sequence can touch the blocks
+	 * outside the DT-defined sub-ranges. */
+	if (avd->variant->revision == 3) {
+		avd->full = devm_ioremap(avd->dev, AVD_FULL_BASE_PHYS,
+					 AVD_FULL_SIZE);
+		if (!avd->full)
+			dev_warn(avd->dev, "AVDBG: full aperture map failed\n");
+	}
+
 	avd->domain = iommu_get_domain_for_dev(avd->dev);
 	if (avd->domain) {
 		avd->empty_domain = iommu_paging_domain_alloc(avd->dev);
